      "category" : "Drug Industry - C0022",
      "comment" : "I am submitting a full comment as an attached PDF regarding Docket No. FDA-2026-N-4390, &ldquo;AI-Enabled Optimization of Early-Phase Clinical Trials Pilot Program.&rdquo;<br/><br/>My comment recommends that FDA consider a modular, sponsor-specific AI architecture rather than a one-size-fits-all AI model. Different therapeutic modalities generate different clinical signals, and early-phase trials may benefit most when sponsors can develop therapy-specific AI modules that connect to FDA-compatible data environments and report predefined safety and efficacy signals in a transparent, auditable, and explainable manner.<br/><br/>The attached comment also describes how an intratumoral oncology therapy may require AI workflows for lesion-level radiology extraction, target lesion identification, anatomic risk flagging, physician-reviewed dose-planning support, early imaging endpoint organization, local safety monitoring, and continuous trial data collection.<br/><br/>Respectfully submitted,<br/>Xuewu Liu<br/>Founder, SunGlow Innovations, LLC",
